<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila eyes $2 bln worth jvs with U.S. firms.</title>
<headline>Manila eyes $2 bln worth jvs with U.S. firms.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>At least $2 billion worth of joint ventures and investments with U.S. companies will be signed next week, Philippine trade and industry secretary Cesar Bautista said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He said the major projects include an electronic manufacturing plant to be set up by Seagate Technologies Inc and a freight forwarding venture to be jointly operated by United Parcel Service and a local firm.</p>
<p>Edna Espos, director of the Bureau of International Trade Relations, said the agreements would enhance bilateral trade between the two countries.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
